 - 2026-10-13: FPS hitches (UNVERIFIED on a device, no toolchain in the session). The 60-117 ms gaps in `Record_2026-10-12-20-37-27` fit meshing two chunks in one frame on a weak phone (a mesh now also samples the climate noise for the biome tints). `ChunkManager::update` times its stages: a second mesh in a frame starts only while the frame's chunk work is under `CHUNK_WORK_BUDGET` (6 ms), so a slow phone builds one chunk per frame and a fast one two; `LIGHT_BUDGET` 10 -> 4 ms (a new chunk lights a few frames later, no frame spends 10 ms on it). A frame whose chunk work takes 16 ms or more logs `slow chunk work` with its stages (stream + populate / light / meshes): if hitches remain, `adb logcat | grep 'slow chunk work'` says which stage. Autosave is NOT the cause that is fixed here: writing chunks eagerly would rewrite each one up to 4 times (`put_region` dirties the 2x2). Next step if one mesh alone is still too slow: mesh on the workers (neighbour blocks behind an `Arc`).
